<title>BRAZIL: Brazil net dollar inflows at $279.2 mln Dec 30.</title>
<headline>Brazil net dollar inflows at $279.2 mln Dec 30.</headline>
<dateline>SAO PAULO 1996-12-31</dateline>
<text>
<p>Preliminary figures for Brazil's commercial and financial foreign exchange contracts showed a $279.2 million surplus on December 30 in the commercial forex market, according to Central Bank data supplied to banks.</p>
<p>A banker with access to the figures said the central bank issued the following breakdown.</p>
<p>DOLLAR FLOWS ON DECEMBER 30</p>
<p>Exports: $434.3 million</p>
<p>Imports: $187 million</p>
<p>Financial buy: $526.4 million</p>
<p>Financial sell: $494.5 million</p>
<p>Surplus: $279.2 million</p>
<p>DECEMBER DOLLAR FLOWS UP TO DATE</p>
<p>Exports: $4.487 billion</p>
<p>Imports: $4.242 billion</p>
<p>Financial buy: $9.894 billion</p>
<p>Financial sell: $6.878 billion</p>
<p>Net surplus: $3.261 billion</p>
<p>Note: the figures were rounded off.</p>
<p>((-- Alexandre Caverni, Sao Paulo Newsroom, 5511 2485415))</p>
</text>
